WEBVTT

00:20.220 --> 00:21.160
Stay back!

00:33.100 --> 00:34.580
He should've said "heel".

00:57.680 --> 00:58.360
Slag it!

01:02.320 --> 01:06.240
- He's really got a delicate touch, Dee Dee.
- Delicate like a moose, Dee Dee.

01:09.520 --> 01:13.040
I hate ripping this heavy junk.
Give me cash cards any day.

01:14.660 --> 01:18.240
Zip it, Bonk.
The plan is get in and get out, fast.

01:21.520 --> 01:24.760
It's a school night, boys and girls.
I'm gonna have to call your folks.

01:50.740 --> 01:52.240
Bonk! Don't!

01:53.120 --> 01:54.520
Yeah, Bonk.
Don't.

03:22.220 --> 03:24.520
Let's go!
Dee Dee, open the door.

03:24.560 --> 03:25.380
On the double.

03:55.780 --> 03:56.700
Incoming!

04:06.600 --> 04:08.700
Bonk! You moron!
Get back here!

04:52.720 --> 04:54.500
You got a death wish, Bats!

04:54.640 --> 04:57.240
And here I thought I was
just being a good citizen.

05:02.460 --> 05:03.400
Got you, sis!

05:13.360 --> 05:14.760
Flagpole.

05:15.220 --> 05:16.200
What did you say?

05:16.480 --> 05:17.860
Flagpole.

05:32.700 --> 05:33.340
Come on!

06:02.740 --> 06:04.840
That ain't coming
out of my allowance.

08:26.360 --> 08:28.020
Still got it.

08:39.940 --> 08:41.740
How did it go with the Jokerz?

08:42.480 --> 08:44.480
I broke up the robbery,
but it was weird.

08:46.150 --> 08:49.500
Third time this month that particular gang
was trying to intercept high-tech machinery.

08:49.840 --> 08:51.190
Jokerz don't use that stuff.

08:51.620 --> 08:55.080
They're probably fencing it.
Corporate espionage is big business.

08:55.660 --> 08:57.840
I may as well sit tight until
I can get another shot at them.

08:59.960 --> 09:01.090
Hey, lookie here.

09:01.480 --> 09:02.360
That's right, Tom.

09:02.600 --> 09:05.935
Today, Gotham billionaire Bruce Wayne
stunned the financial world...

09:05.960 --> 09:09.360
...with his plan to resume
active leadership of Wayne Enterprises.

09:09.680 --> 09:12.600
While shareholders have generally
welcomed Wayne's return...

09:12.780 --> 09:16.440
...support from some key members
of the Wayne board has been oddly lukewarm.

09:16.720 --> 09:20.200
Company operations manager,
Jordan Pryce, offered this comment:

09:20.300 --> 09:23.320
I, of course, join the rest of our
Wayne Enterprises family...

09:23.360 --> 09:27.620
...in welcoming back our most valuable
senior resource, Bruce Wayne.

09:27.840 --> 09:31.160
I'm sure we'll all profit
from his years of experience.

09:31.340 --> 09:35.215
Still, the day to day rigors of running
a vast, multinational conglomerate...

09:35.240 --> 09:37.290
...would be stressful,
even for a young man.

09:37.560 --> 09:39.780
I hope Mr. Wayne is up
to the challenge.

09:40.000 --> 09:41.700
He's not bitter,
much.

09:42.200 --> 09:44.440
Pryce was next in line
for the top spot.

09:44.940 --> 09:47.870
My return torpedoed any dreams
he had of succession.

09:48.640 --> 09:51.640
- You gonna keep him around?
- If he'll stay on my terms.

09:52.000 --> 09:55.550
I've worked long and hard to regain control
of my family's company.

09:55.840 --> 09:57.310
And I won't hand it over again.

09:57.560 --> 10:01.520
Pryce can either get with that program
or start e-mailing his résumé.

10:01.820 --> 10:04.240
With all the long hours you're planning
on putting in at the office...

10:04.460 --> 10:07.000
...does this mean
you'll have less time for...

10:07.300 --> 10:08.800
Who sleeps anymore?

10:12.520 --> 10:13.320
You okay?

10:13.500 --> 10:15.600
You know the Jokerz
are going in for splicing now.

10:15.880 --> 10:20.080
Crazy hyena-boy nearly took a bite out of me.
No way I could have explained that to Dana.

10:20.340 --> 10:21.600
You're not going out now?

10:21.820 --> 10:23.420
The night is young and so am I.

10:23.700 --> 10:26.300
I think a good night's rest
might be more beneficial.

10:26.580 --> 10:28.900
Like you said,
who sleeps anymore?

10:37.430 --> 10:39.160
Up and at them, Terry.

10:41.600 --> 10:44.400
You can doze on Bruce Wayne's time,
not mine.

10:44.970 --> 10:46.370
Sorry, Dane.

11:12.830 --> 11:14.490
Great song, huh?

11:15.900 --> 11:19.200
Did you see the squid Blade's with? P.U.!

11:21.270 --> 11:23.000
Ter, my head's on fire.

11:23.780 --> 11:24.840
You look good.

11:25.720 --> 11:26.830
McGinnis!

11:32.050 --> 11:35.100
Sorry, babe. Guess the day
was longer than I thought.

11:38.160 --> 11:39.680
Let's sit this one out.

11:41.320 --> 11:43.620
Coffee,
And leave the pot.

11:48.380 --> 11:50.360
Batman showed up
and we had to ditch.

11:50.680 --> 11:54.530
We were able to save this:
the console's memory board.

11:55.900 --> 11:57.200
I know it's not much but--

11:57.800 --> 12:01.000
It's not much?
It's nothing.

12:03.650 --> 12:05.110
Losers.

12:06.020 --> 12:07.060
All of you.

12:07.150 --> 12:11.420
A disgrace to the name Joker.
Why, in my day--

12:11.460 --> 12:12.790
In your day?!

12:13.040 --> 12:15.275
Ever since you conned
your way into this gang...

12:15.300 --> 12:18.360
...it's been "your day" this
and "your day" that.

12:18.660 --> 12:19.600
Bonk.

12:19.820 --> 12:21.495
Your day is over, old man.

12:21.520 --> 12:25.760
Even if you are who you say you are.
And personally, I think you're a fake.

12:26.020 --> 12:28.670
Ah,
brave new world...

12:28.820 --> 12:31.140
...that has such putzes in it.

12:31.620 --> 12:35.340
He's got us running around ripping
a lot of geek junk, but no cash!

12:35.940 --> 12:38.910
He won't tell us what his plan is,
if he even has one.

12:39.160 --> 12:41.050
I want out!

12:41.320 --> 12:43.020
If you insist.

12:46.660 --> 12:50.000
Hey, man. Take it easy.
I was just kidding.

12:53.600 --> 12:55.220
So was I.

13:05.300 --> 13:07.800
Oops.
No, I wasn't.

13:09.810 --> 13:12.500
That's also how
we did it in my day.

13:15.060 --> 13:19.020
You know, kids, a lot has changed
while your old Uncle Joker's been away.

13:19.120 --> 13:21.680
New Gotham,
new rules...

13:21.740 --> 13:24.060
...even a new Batman.

13:26.230 --> 13:28.630
But now I'm tanned,
I'm rested...

13:28.680 --> 13:32.880
...and I'm ready to give
this old town a wedgie again!

13:33.620 --> 13:35.140
I have to know
you're with me.

13:35.300 --> 13:38.620
- Will you say it for me one time?
- We're with you!

13:38.980 --> 13:42.040
- Little louder.
- We're with you!

13:42.220 --> 13:44.300
- Dee Dee?
- We're with you!

13:44.560 --> 13:47.860
- Boys?
- We're with you!

13:48.380 --> 13:49.300
- Bonk?

13:50.480 --> 13:51.690
Oh, right.

13:51.780 --> 13:52.260
Dead.

13:53.460 --> 13:55.900
Dee Dee, be lamb
and sweep out the trash.

13:56.320 --> 13:58.000
There's good girls.

14:02.040 --> 14:05.840
Your renewed faith
puts a smile in my heart.

14:05.920 --> 14:09.070
What say we forget tonight's misshapen
and start over...

14:09.520 --> 14:10.980
Great, boss.

14:11.220 --> 14:15.100
Ghoul, my boy, we're going
to need another systems scanner.

14:15.140 --> 14:17.540
Who's got one
they'd be willing to donate?

14:17.620 --> 14:19.060
Checking.

14:19.380 --> 14:21.620
What we're after
is cutting-edge.

14:21.880 --> 14:24.120
These are the only other places
we'd find one.

14:25.100 --> 14:26.020
Nope.

14:26.120 --> 14:26.900
Uh uh.

14:27.000 --> 14:27.580
No.

14:29.200 --> 14:32.060
What, there?
Security's gonna be tight!

14:32.760 --> 14:35.480
Oh, yes.
But think of the fun.

14:41.920 --> 14:43.140
Good evening, Mr. Wayne.

14:43.600 --> 14:46.500
Ms. Carr. You remember
my assistant, Terry McGinnis?

14:46.700 --> 14:48.920
Of course. I'm glad
you could join us, Terry.

14:50.100 --> 14:54.200
Everyone is here. Well, everyone
except Mr. Pryce, unfortunately.

14:54.560 --> 14:55.960
That's no surprise.

14:57.240 --> 14:58.900
May I have
your attention, please?

14:59.320 --> 15:04.100
It's my pleasure to welcome back
the guiding light of this company:

15:04.580 --> 15:05.560
Bruce Wayne.

15:13.180 --> 15:14.420
Thank you, Joyce.

15:14.940 --> 15:18.340
It's a pleasure to see you all again.
In the future, I hope to--

15:26.540 --> 15:29.360
--spend time getting to know
each member of our company...

15:29.920 --> 15:31.620
...learning about
you individually--

15:53.640 --> 15:54.480
Security!

15:54.520 --> 15:56.120
Emergency on terrace level.

16:01.540 --> 16:02.780
Hey! Look out!

16:18.500 --> 16:20.500
- You gonna be okay?
- Go to work.

16:23.580 --> 16:25.580
Well, if it isn't old Mr. Wayne.

16:26.500 --> 16:27.680
So debonair.

16:28.560 --> 16:29.660
So dapper.

16:31.720 --> 16:32.940
So decrepit.

16:46.760 --> 16:48.160
Hello, Gotham!

16:48.280 --> 16:50.260
Joker's back in town!

16:53.160 --> 16:54.640
It can't be.

16:54.820 --> 16:59.140
Oh, no, your old eyes
do not deceive you, Brucie!

16:59.240 --> 17:02.060
After all, who'd know me
better than you?

17:04.920 --> 17:06.120
Back off, gruesome.

17:10.260 --> 17:12.380
Ah, the new boy.

17:12.460 --> 17:14.775
Ears are too long
and I miss the cape...

17:14.800 --> 17:17.700
...but not too shabby.
Not too shabby at all.

17:17.880 --> 17:18.460
Woof!

17:30.700 --> 17:33.920
- How's it coming, boys?
- We're home free.

17:34.080 --> 17:35.480
Then I'll see you there.

17:40.200 --> 17:42.100
Time to go, Dee Dee.

18:19.380 --> 18:21.600
Well?
What's it gonna be, Bat-fake?

18:51.670 --> 18:54.160
I know what you're thinking.
I messed up.

18:54.770 --> 18:56.970
I let the clown go
in order to save those people.

18:57.340 --> 18:58.710
You did the right thing.

18:59.400 --> 19:04.040
So, the Joker, huh? Looks pretty spry
for a guy who's gotta be, what?

19:04.260 --> 19:05.510
Mid-eighties?

19:07.360 --> 19:08.760
Any theories on that?

19:09.290 --> 19:10.280
Clone?

19:10.760 --> 19:11.720
Robot?

19:12.060 --> 19:15.540
Suspended animation due to floating
around frozen in a block of ice?

19:15.830 --> 19:17.320
Shut up and drive.

19:19.060 --> 19:20.050
Yes, sir.

19:27.340 --> 19:31.980
This was the scene just three hours ago,
as a man claiming to be the legendary Joker...

19:32.020 --> 19:35.850
...disrupted a ceremony at the newly
opened Wayne Enterprises building.

19:35.980 --> 19:37.570
Honey, what are you watching?

19:37.780 --> 19:41.900
Adding to the drama was the appearance of
another legendary Gotham icon, the Batman...

19:41.940 --> 19:45.190
...who engaged his one-time foe
in a stunning aerial battle.

19:45.600 --> 19:46.560
Honey?

19:46.860 --> 19:48.260
It's nothing, sweetheart.

19:50.800 --> 19:51.720
Nothing.

20:01.680 --> 20:02.600
Go away.

20:03.020 --> 20:03.930
Morning, commish.

20:04.140 --> 20:06.680
You understand English, McGinnis?
Scram.

20:07.060 --> 20:10.160
Love to. But first, what can you
tell me about clowns?

20:10.620 --> 20:12.500
In this town
they're never funny.

20:13.020 --> 20:14.180
I noticed that.

20:17.440 --> 20:19.500
- Now, this Joker--
- Drop it, kid.

20:19.840 --> 20:22.620
- That's what the old man's been saying.
- Listen to him.

20:23.020 --> 20:26.960
Hey look, I know this fruitcake was one of the
big bad guy from the cape and cowl days.

20:27.260 --> 20:28.560
He was more than that.

20:28.800 --> 20:31.480
What? A garden-variety wacko
who threatened people...

20:31.520 --> 20:33.600
...with whoopee cushions
and squirting flowers?

20:33.920 --> 20:35.900
- Big deal. I'm shaking.
- McGinnis!

20:40.480 --> 20:43.875
The Joker, the real Joker,
was unlike anyone you've ever faced.

20:43.900 --> 20:45.720
And for your sake,
I hope you never do.

20:45.960 --> 20:48.340
If Bruce wants you to drop it,
then drop it.

20:49.960 --> 20:52.900
- Commissioner, your 9 o'clock is here.
- Send him in.

20:53.560 --> 20:54.550
You were leaving?

20:55.080 --> 20:56.200
Figure I was.

21:08.320 --> 21:11.500
- Thanks for seeing me, Barb.
- That's what I'm here for.

21:32.260 --> 21:35.100
--a countdown of victims
that will end at midnight...

21:35.240 --> 21:38.260
...unless our dear Dark Knight
stops me first!

21:42.660 --> 21:45.700
Hello, Gotham!
Joker's back in town!

21:54.440 --> 21:55.600
It's funny.

21:55.960 --> 21:59.100
I know about all of your other major enemies
but you never mentioned him.

21:59.840 --> 22:03.700
- He was the biggest, wasn't he?
- It wasn't a popularity contest.

22:04.260 --> 22:07.000
He was a psychopath.
A monster.

22:07.440 --> 22:10.500
So how is it possible he could still
be around after all this time?

22:10.940 --> 22:12.380
It's not possible.

22:12.620 --> 22:14.320
He died years ago.

22:14.900 --> 22:15.820
You're sure?

22:16.060 --> 22:17.340
I was there.

22:21.640 --> 22:23.420
You killed him, didn't you?

22:25.510 --> 22:28.240
He was gonna do something so terrible,
you had no other choice.

22:28.680 --> 22:31.070
- Terry--
- That was it, wasn't it?

22:35.110 --> 22:37.580
I want you to give back
the Batman suit.

22:38.040 --> 22:40.040
What? Why?

22:40.320 --> 22:42.600
There is no reason for you to continue.

22:43.180 --> 22:45.640
You've made your father's killers
pay for his murder...

22:45.980 --> 22:50.120
...then put your own needs aside to help
the city when it most needed a hero.

22:50.840 --> 22:55.140
You've honored the reputation of Batman
many times over and for that I thank you.

22:55.280 --> 22:56.220
Then why?

22:57.000 --> 23:00.500
I had no right to force this life
on you or anyone else.

23:01.100 --> 23:04.060
Hey, i was the one who broke in
and swiped the suit, remember?

23:04.740 --> 23:08.770
Yes, there was my dad's murder,
but we come from two different worlds, Mr. Wayne.

23:09.020 --> 23:11.280
I wasn't like you
or the kids you took in.

23:12.840 --> 23:14.940
I was a pretty bad kid once.

23:15.240 --> 23:18.950
Ran with a rough crowd, broke a lot of laws,
to say nothing to my folks' hearts.

23:19.580 --> 23:22.720
The kind of punk you wouldn't have
wasted a second punch on back in the day.

23:23.280 --> 23:24.380
Your point?

23:24.860 --> 23:27.230
I'm trying to make up
for past sins.

23:28.060 --> 23:31.630
The state says my 3 months in juvie
wiped me clean, but my soul tells me different.

23:32.270 --> 23:36.080
Every time I put on that suit is my chance
to help people who are in trouble.

23:37.180 --> 23:39.200
I guess on a personal level...

23:39.540 --> 23:42.460
...it's a chance to look like
a worthwhile human being again.

23:42.920 --> 23:45.000
In my eyes,
if no one else's.

23:46.840 --> 23:48.460
It's what I want, Bruce.

23:50.990 --> 23:52.080
Stupid kid.

23:52.590 --> 23:55.720
You don't know what you want.
None of you ever did.

24:29.730 --> 24:33.080
Mom, come quick!
Some weirdo broke into our house!

24:33.400 --> 24:37.600
- Matty? What are you yelling about?
- There's a stranger sitting at our table!

24:37.900 --> 24:40.000
- Ha, ha.
- That's your brother.

24:42.440 --> 24:44.310
I've never seen him
before in my life.

24:44.400 --> 24:48.380
It is rare that you're up and around before noon, Terry
what with your job and all.

24:48.740 --> 24:51.100
I'm not working for
Mr. Wayne anymore.

24:53.600 --> 24:57.020
Well, it will be nice to have you home
for a change. Right, Matt?

24:57.260 --> 25:00.890
Sure. Great. Just when I was
getting used to being an only child.

25:03.300 --> 25:04.390
Mom!

25:11.040 --> 25:15.140
Every once in a while, we have to do it, Dane.
Ditch the guys and have a night out to ourselves.

25:15.220 --> 25:19.440
It may be a change for you, Chelsea.
I don't see enough of Terry to know the difference.

25:19.500 --> 25:23.320
Well, Terry's sweet and all, but who says
you can't make friends with someone new?

25:23.530 --> 25:24.580
Not a chance.

25:24.890 --> 25:25.820
Terry!

25:27.260 --> 25:29.200
I thought you'd be
working as usual.

25:30.540 --> 25:33.400
The bad news is, for the time being,
I'm not gonna have much money coming in.

25:34.040 --> 25:36.600
The good news is,
you have me all to yourself.

25:37.210 --> 25:38.500
I can live with that.

25:53.050 --> 25:54.000
Cutting in.

25:58.860 --> 25:59.780
Hey!

26:06.370 --> 26:07.240
Dana?

26:22.380 --> 26:23.140
What is it, boy?

26:25.350 --> 26:25.980
Ace.

26:29.930 --> 26:30.780
Ace!

26:58.920 --> 27:03.820
Don't get up, Bruce.
It's just an old friend come by to say hello.

27:11.930 --> 27:13.230
Hello...

27:13.630 --> 27:15.100
...Batman.

27:20.480 --> 27:21.700
Dana!

27:24.980 --> 27:25.720
It was her.

27:48.260 --> 27:50.855
Don’t know why the boss
wants a dreg like you outta the way, but...

27:50.880 --> 27:52.800
...hey, as long as it's fun.

27:56.800 --> 27:57.680
Terry!

27:59.600 --> 28:00.360
Dana!

28:03.470 --> 28:06.180
- Let me go!
- Sure, cutes.

28:13.180 --> 28:14.400
Slag him!

28:29.020 --> 28:31.000
- Dana?
- Stay out of sight!

28:50.920 --> 28:51.560
There!

29:05.200 --> 29:06.400
What's he doing?

29:06.580 --> 29:07.800
You got me.

29:09.000 --> 29:10.360
Just finish him!

29:30.380 --> 29:32.800
Ah, you made a mess, dreg.

29:44.320 --> 29:44.940
Dana!

29:45.180 --> 29:48.500
She's got a bad bump and some cuts,
but she's gonna be okay.

29:49.140 --> 29:51.880
- Why were those guys after you?
- I don't know.

29:52.320 --> 29:55.040
Look, I'm gonna talk to the cops.
Stay with her, okay, Chels?

29:55.080 --> 29:57.000
- I'll come as soon as I can.
- Sure.

30:13.940 --> 30:15.080
Leave a message.

30:15.520 --> 30:18.140
Hey, the Joker's little playmates
were after me tonight.

30:18.180 --> 30:19.720
Me, not Batman.

30:20.040 --> 30:22.140
This whole thing stinks, Wayne,
and you know why.

30:22.210 --> 30:27.160
I need some straight answers from--
Wait, it's night. Where does he go?

30:48.440 --> 30:49.380
Wayne?

30:49.800 --> 30:50.460
Wayne!

30:55.860 --> 30:56.840
Ace.

31:11.600 --> 31:13.200
Please, God, no.

31:42.240 --> 31:43.680
Floor...

31:46.990 --> 31:49.140
...under...

31:50.800 --> 31:52.880
...table.

32:27.740 --> 32:28.690
How is he?

32:29.080 --> 32:32.360
The anti-toxin's done all it can.
It's up to him now.

32:32.760 --> 32:35.300
Thanks for coming.
I didn't know who else to call.

32:35.500 --> 32:36.480
Who else is there?

32:37.080 --> 32:40.000
That reminds me.
I'd better check on our other patient.

32:43.050 --> 32:44.600
What have I done?

32:45.650 --> 32:48.200
I killed the little rabbit!

32:49.060 --> 32:52.000
I don't deserve to live!

32:56.540 --> 32:58.660
I wish i were dead!

32:58.700 --> 33:00.100
How you doing, killer?

33:03.910 --> 33:05.740
Yeah, rough night for me too.

33:06.700 --> 33:08.860
Sad news from the financial world
this morning:

33:08.940 --> 33:13.500
The return of Bruce Wayne to his family's company
has been delayed due to an accident.

33:13.620 --> 33:16.500
Wayne Enterprises' Jordan Pryce
had this to say:

33:16.720 --> 33:20.240
We received a call from
Mr. Wayne's houseboy this morning...

33:20.280 --> 33:22.780
...saying Mr. Wayne
had taken a bad fall.

33:23.240 --> 33:27.280
Everyone at the Wayne Enterprises' family
sends their prayers and good wishes...

33:27.320 --> 33:30.480
...to our senior member
for his speedy recovery.

33:31.640 --> 33:32.600
I'll bet.

33:33.120 --> 33:35.200
Not every creep in Gotham
wears a purple suit.

33:35.420 --> 33:37.300
It'd make my job simpler
if they did.

33:37.670 --> 33:41.610
The Joker knew about Bruce, about me,
probably about you too.

33:42.140 --> 33:43.770
Someone knows,
I'll give you that.

33:44.160 --> 33:46.860
But it's not the Joker.
Not the real one.

33:47.520 --> 33:48.700
Bruce said he was dead.

33:50.780 --> 33:51.500
And?

33:51.820 --> 33:52.600
That's it.

33:53.220 --> 33:54.600
I know there's more.

33:55.190 --> 33:58.420
Barbara, I'm a part of this.
I need the answers Bruce can't give me.

33:59.060 --> 34:00.320
I deserve them.

34:06.700 --> 34:09.280
I thought talking about it
would get easier over time...

34:09.540 --> 34:11.440
...but some hurts
never go away.

34:12.860 --> 34:15.315
Dick Grayson,
Nightwing, had left...

34:15.340 --> 34:17.420
...to establish himself
in another city.

34:18.540 --> 34:22.300
There were three of us then:
Bruce, myself and Robin, Tim Drake.

34:32.540 --> 34:36.000
Robin was out alone that night
when he came upon a woman in trouble.

34:36.760 --> 34:38.600
Help! Help!

34:39.030 --> 34:41.100
Somebody, please, help!

34:43.910 --> 34:45.000
Hero time.

34:51.750 --> 34:55.280
- That evens things up a little.
- Not really, bird-boy!

35:03.540 --> 35:05.320
A bird in the hand.

35:08.260 --> 35:10.250
We soon realized
Tim was missing.

35:12.320 --> 35:16.400
Night after night we scoured the city,
running down every lead...

35:16.600 --> 35:19.000
...pressing every underworld connection.

35:22.680 --> 35:25.300
But no one had seen
any sign of Robin.

35:26.140 --> 35:29.340
For three agonizing weeks
there was nothing.

35:29.650 --> 35:33.000
Then one night,
we were sent an invitation.

36:03.680 --> 36:04.640
Arkham.

36:06.620 --> 36:09.500
The asylum had been moved
to a newer, high-security building.

36:10.100 --> 36:12.700
The old building had been
partially demolished...

36:12.740 --> 36:15.240
...and hung open,
like a rotting wound.

36:22.240 --> 36:26.500
Hush, little baby, don't say a word

36:26.620 --> 36:30.980
Mama's gonna buy you a mockingbird

36:31.120 --> 36:35.700
And if that mockingbird don't sing

36:35.940 --> 36:40.400
Mama's gonna buy you a diamond ring

36:40.660 --> 36:45.600
And if that diamond ring turns brass

36:45.840 --> 36:50.770
Mama's gonna buy you a looking glass

36:50.860 --> 36:56.000
And if that looking glass gets broke

36:57.840 --> 36:59.660
Pudding, company!

37:02.540 --> 37:06.160
Hello there!
Welcome to our happy home.

37:10.800 --> 37:11.940
Where's Robin?

37:12.860 --> 37:14.010
Robin?

37:14.390 --> 37:15.980
There's no Robin here.

37:16.020 --> 37:18.120
Maybe he means our little J.

37:18.460 --> 37:20.200
Of course! That's it!

37:25.620 --> 37:28.000
Uh uh, no peeking.

37:36.860 --> 37:38.680
Mommy's little helper.

37:41.740 --> 37:45.780
You know, Bats, we've been doing
this little run around of ours for years.

37:45.960 --> 37:49.110
It's been loads of laughs,
but the sad fact is...

37:49.360 --> 37:51.220
...none of us
are getting any younger.

37:51.500 --> 37:53.450
That old clock's a-ticking.

37:53.640 --> 37:55.180
Quite right, pooh.

37:55.560 --> 37:59.000
And Harley and I were thinking
it was time to start a family.

37:59.180 --> 38:02.260
Add a Joker Junior
to our merry brood.

38:02.720 --> 38:05.740
But rather than go through
all the joy of childbirth...

38:06.060 --> 38:07.620
...we decided to adopt.

38:10.160 --> 38:11.960
We couldn't do it legally...

38:12.000 --> 38:16.480
...but then we remembered you always
had a few spare kids hanging around.

38:16.680 --> 38:18.400
So we borrowed one.

38:22.890 --> 38:23.880
No.

38:24.090 --> 38:25.720
My God!

38:26.030 --> 38:30.490
He needed a little molding of course.
What kid doesn't?

38:30.700 --> 38:33.890
But in time,
we came to love him as our own.

38:34.040 --> 38:36.570
Say hello, J.J.

39:08.960 --> 39:10.360
Robin! Robin!

39:13.480 --> 39:16.800
Tim, it's Barbara.
Can you hear me?

39:30.500 --> 39:32.160
Robin! Stop!

39:33.300 --> 39:35.440
Hands off, Brat-girl!

39:35.600 --> 39:38.100
Sweetie, get Mommy's bazooka.

40:06.820 --> 40:08.850
How could you help
Joker do it, Harley?

40:09.200 --> 40:12.700
Okay, so he roughed the kid up a little,
but I'll make it right.

40:13.260 --> 40:15.780
Yeah, you're mother
of the stinking year.

40:16.000 --> 40:17.420
Ha! You'll see.

40:19.480 --> 40:22.220
We'll be one big, happy family.

40:28.980 --> 40:29.930
Good boy!

41:20.500 --> 41:22.150
What's the matter, Batman?

41:22.720 --> 41:25.280
No witty comeback?
No threat?

41:26.120 --> 41:28.240
Then I'll provide the narration.

41:39.540 --> 41:44.000
I'll begin with how I peeled back
the layers of the boy's mind.

41:46.060 --> 41:48.660
Though, he bravely
tried to fight it at first.

42:00.500 --> 42:03.980
You would have been proud
to see him so strong!

42:05.800 --> 42:07.420
But all too soon...

42:07.540 --> 42:10.720
...the serums and the shocks
took their toll...

42:11.120 --> 42:15.500
...and the dear lad began
to share such secrets with me.

42:15.820 --> 42:19.200
Secrets that are
mine alone to know...

42:19.480 --> 42:21.080
...Bruce.

42:21.400 --> 42:24.680
It's true, Batsy.
I know everything.

42:24.810 --> 42:27.900
And kind of like the kid
who peeks at his Christmas presents...

42:28.040 --> 42:31.620
...I must admit,
it's sadly anticlimactic.

42:31.810 --> 42:34.780
Behind all the
Sturm and batarangs...

42:34.820 --> 42:39.660
...you're just a little boy in a play-suit,
crying for Mommy and Daddy.

42:39.820 --> 42:42.300
It'd be funny,
if it weren't so pathetic.

42:43.980 --> 42:46.540
Oh, what the heck!
I'll laugh anyway.

43:01.180 --> 43:04.440
If you don't like the movie,
I've got slides.

43:16.400 --> 43:18.880
I'll break you in two.

43:19.060 --> 43:20.550
Oh, Batman.

43:20.580 --> 43:24.680
If you had the guts for that kind of fun,
you'd have done it years ago.

43:24.780 --> 43:26.960
I, on the other hand...

43:37.780 --> 43:39.620
You've lost, Batman.

43:39.960 --> 43:41.500
Robin is mine.

43:41.740 --> 43:45.650
The last sound you hear
will be our laughter.

43:48.240 --> 43:49.880
Here you go, sonny-boy.

43:53.080 --> 43:57.140
Make daddy proud.
Deliver the punch line.

44:04.840 --> 44:05.860
Tim.

44:12.580 --> 44:13.420
Do it!

44:20.340 --> 44:23.520
That's not funny.
That's not--

44:48.840 --> 44:51.600
It's okay, Tim.
It's okay.

44:51.980 --> 44:54.180
We buried the Joker
deep beneath Arkham.

44:54.900 --> 44:59.120
The only other person who knew what happened that night
was my father, the first commissioner Gordon.

44:59.600 --> 45:01.100
He promised
to keep our secret.

45:03.480 --> 45:05.540
With his last act of cruelty...

45:05.600 --> 45:09.700
...the Joker had tainted us all
with compromise and deception.

45:13.600 --> 45:15.900
I suppose he had
the last laugh after all.

45:16.320 --> 45:18.200
I'm assuming his girlfriend
bought it too.

45:18.380 --> 45:21.780
We never found her body,
but I doubt she'd be starting trouble now.

45:24.610 --> 45:25.400
And Tim?

45:25.480 --> 45:28.160
We had a trusted friend,
Dr. Leslie Thompkins.

45:28.260 --> 45:31.500
It took her a year, but she was able
to help Tim back to sanity.

45:32.180 --> 45:34.700
Still, things were never
really the same.

45:35.000 --> 45:37.360
Bruce forbade Tim
to be Robin again.

45:37.720 --> 45:42.180
He blamed himself for what happened
and swore he'd never endanger another young partner.

45:42.740 --> 45:46.200
Tim left us soon after that,
determined to make it on his own.

45:46.700 --> 45:48.000
Did they patch things up?

45:48.260 --> 45:52.800
Tim tried once or twice, but you know Bruce.
I check up on Tim now and then.

45:53.020 --> 45:56.680
He's a top-level communications engineer,
married, couple kids.

45:57.200 --> 45:59.100
Not too bad,
all things concerned.

45:59.420 --> 46:00.900
He deserved a happy ending.

46:01.600 --> 46:04.000
But he still has the most likely
connection to that night.

46:14.110 --> 46:16.720
It looks okay on this side.
I'm going up to the dish.

46:28.820 --> 46:31.800
You might as well show yourself.
I heard you a mile away.

46:33.330 --> 46:37.000
I'm no Boy Wonder anymore,
but that old training never goes away.

46:37.130 --> 46:38.400
...even at my age.

46:39.320 --> 46:40.300
Tim Drake.

46:40.830 --> 46:42.100
You heard about Bruce?

46:42.680 --> 46:45.180
Barbara told me.
That was too bad.

46:45.440 --> 46:46.880
You're not too broken up.

46:47.170 --> 46:49.820
I had nothing to do with it,
despite what you might be thinking.

46:50.100 --> 46:53.280
When the Joker reappeared,
I was just as surprised as anyone.

46:53.680 --> 46:55.860
Barb told you the gory details?

46:56.310 --> 46:57.540
More or less.

46:57.850 --> 47:00.000
Look, it's been
almost 40 years.

47:00.250 --> 47:03.740
It wasn't easy, but I managed
to put it to bed and go on with my life.

47:04.020 --> 47:07.700
You'll have to do it yourself one day.
We all did.

47:08.220 --> 47:11.890
We gave our best, but in the end,
that wasn't good enough for the old man.

47:12.670 --> 47:14.100
Regrets, Mr. Drake?

47:15.030 --> 47:18.600
When I was younger, part of me thought
I would go on and on and someday...

47:19.740 --> 47:23.020
Capes, costumes, playing hero.
It was kids' stuff.

47:23.520 --> 47:25.310
Bruce probably did me a favor.

47:25.510 --> 47:29.480
In the end I was so sick of it,
I never wanted to see that stupid Robin suit again.

47:32.550 --> 47:34.260
Some things never change.

47:36.400 --> 47:38.500
Were all of you that bitter
when you left?

47:38.840 --> 47:40.620
Comes with the territory, McGinnis.

47:40.920 --> 47:43.180
Look up Nightwing, someday.
Has he got stories!

47:43.480 --> 47:46.440
Drake's clean anyway.
I've got one more lead to check out.

47:46.480 --> 47:49.020
Someone with a definite grudge
to hold against Bruce Wayne.

48:06.340 --> 48:09.540
Caviar, soft music
and charming company.

48:09.960 --> 48:12.220
Amy, my dear,
I can't think of any better way...

48:12.260 --> 48:15.600
...to celebrate my ascension
to CEO of Wayne Enterprises.

48:16.200 --> 48:18.300
- Me neither.
- Me neither.

48:22.780 --> 48:24.460
You? Where's Amy?

48:25.680 --> 48:27.000
Missed the boat, I'm afraid.

48:31.400 --> 48:32.620
Turn the yacht around!

48:32.820 --> 48:36.660
Detox, boss man.
We're here to talk business.

48:36.720 --> 48:40.060
We'll be quick.
Woof gets seasick easy.

48:42.560 --> 48:44.740
Our business is concluded.

48:52.520 --> 48:54.220
You've got the equipment
you wanted.

48:54.360 --> 48:57.880
I gave you the security code
so you could ransack the lab...

48:58.000 --> 49:00.160
...while those bunglers
tried to kill Wayne.

49:01.200 --> 49:03.580
Word is Wayne's terminal anyhow.

49:05.320 --> 49:07.640
That means you get
to stay top dog.

49:07.820 --> 49:09.280
And everyone's happy.

49:09.860 --> 49:11.260
So why are you here?

49:11.380 --> 49:16.000
The big guy who originally put us all in contact
has decided you're a loose end.

49:16.560 --> 49:19.000
And loose ends
should be tied up.

49:26.040 --> 49:27.340
Let me go!

49:28.140 --> 49:29.000
Got him.

49:29.510 --> 49:32.000
Then amscray pronto, kiddies.

49:35.820 --> 49:38.160
Things are going to start popping.

49:38.360 --> 49:39.480
Let's go!

49:41.680 --> 49:43.840
No one's leaving
until I get answers.

49:48.000 --> 49:50.240
No, you idiot!
Not now!

49:59.720 --> 50:01.120
They're getting away!

50:02.110 --> 50:03.800
Yeah, and I think
they've got a good reason!

50:07.250 --> 50:09.120
- What's happening?
- Hang on!

50:52.860 --> 50:54.040
We saw the explosion.

50:54.540 --> 50:56.280
You can ask Mr. Pryce about that.

50:56.820 --> 50:58.980
Me? I had nothing to do with it.

50:59.200 --> 51:00.300
That right?

51:01.220 --> 51:04.600
I gave you the security code
so you could ransack the lab...

51:04.840 --> 51:07.080
...while those bunglers
tried to kill Wayne.

51:07.640 --> 51:08.880
I want my lawyer.

51:08.950 --> 51:12.780
I think the commissioner would like
to hear this too. Night.

51:29.540 --> 51:30.700
I'm spent.

51:31.480 --> 51:34.680
Every lead I had has gone face-down,
and the Joker's still out there.

51:35.180 --> 51:36.300
What have you got?

51:37.420 --> 51:38.580
I don't know, pup.

51:39.090 --> 51:42.100
If I was the Batman I was supposed to be,
I'd have cracked this by now...

51:42.560 --> 51:45.000
...would have punched exactly the right data
into the computer...

51:45.200 --> 51:48.000
...or remembered that one little clue
that everyone else overlooked.

51:48.820 --> 51:50.600
It's rarely that simple.

51:57.420 --> 51:59.680
- How are you feeling?
- Lousy.

52:02.210 --> 52:04.100
Gordon told me what happened
to Tim Drake.

52:04.640 --> 52:07.780
That's why I didn't want you
going up against the Joker...

52:08.280 --> 52:09.800
...impostor or not.

52:10.020 --> 52:13.500
Nothing against your old partners,
but I'm a completely different Batman.

52:13.840 --> 52:15.480
I was never a Robin,
I never--

52:19.160 --> 52:20.000
Wait.

52:21.330 --> 52:23.100
Joker smashed up the cases...

52:23.320 --> 52:26.260
...but why was this the only costume
he went out of his way to destroy?

52:26.570 --> 52:27.900
Robin did shoot him.

52:28.170 --> 52:31.800
A ghost out for revenge? I don't buy it.
I talked to Drake.

52:31.920 --> 52:34.200
He's got less love for that costume
than the Joker.

52:34.840 --> 52:36.600
I think somehow
he's behind this.

52:37.260 --> 52:38.340
That's crazy.

52:38.480 --> 52:40.680
So was Drake, once.

52:40.840 --> 52:44.400
Look, here's the readout of everything
we know the Jokerz have stolen.

52:47.380 --> 52:50.900
Now let's combine those into something
that would be used by a communications expert.

52:51.160 --> 52:52.960
Someone of Tim Drake's caliber.

52:55.700 --> 52:57.500
Satellite jamming system.

52:57.860 --> 53:00.855
Whoever uses this can access
satellite defense systems...

53:00.880 --> 53:02.100
...and fire them at will.

53:02.540 --> 53:04.000
Someone already has.

53:04.140 --> 53:06.300
I suspected Jordan Pryce
might be the Joker...

53:06.440 --> 53:09.300
...but the Jokerz were on your company yacht
trying to slag Pryce.

53:09.580 --> 53:12.220
I got him off the boat
before someone blasted into splinters.

53:15.550 --> 53:18.800
I think your little Robin's
turned into a bitter old crow.

53:19.280 --> 53:21.410
He's gotta be the brains
behind this new Joker.

53:21.600 --> 53:24.200
It's harsh,
but who else is there?

53:26.660 --> 53:27.900
Suit up.

53:28.340 --> 53:31.720
Take the car and check it out.
I'll monitor you from here.

53:33.200 --> 53:34.960
What happened to
leaving it to the cops?

53:36.040 --> 53:37.120
Not their game.

53:37.640 --> 53:40.040
There's something else
I want to take with me.

54:04.500 --> 54:07.260
Drake, I know you're
the connection to the Joker.

54:09.980 --> 54:11.960
Don't pretend
you didn't hear me.

54:12.710 --> 54:13.540
Hologram.

54:28.220 --> 54:30.250
You guessed it, Bat-fake!

54:30.460 --> 54:33.800
The disgruntled Mr. Drake
is indeed in my employ.

54:34.560 --> 54:39.580
Took him a few years, but he finally figured out
who ran the real winning team.

54:39.740 --> 54:43.220
This is one of Uncle Sam's
orbiting defense satellites.

54:43.470 --> 54:46.020
Hyperion class, laser-armed.

54:46.140 --> 54:48.815
Handy little gadget
for shooting down unfriendly missiles...

54:48.840 --> 54:51.680
...or giving someone
a world-class hotfoot.

54:54.120 --> 54:57.440
Think of it as urban tagging
on a grand scale...

54:57.520 --> 55:02.490
...reminding all and sundry
that this is Joker territory.

55:02.740 --> 55:04.750
You're welcome to try
and stop us but...

55:04.940 --> 55:08.800
...I'm not taking bets on that
happening anytime soon. Toodle.

56:02.910 --> 56:03.640
Miss me?

56:13.250 --> 56:15.550
Computer, search
for the name Jolly Jack.

56:21.230 --> 56:24.560
Abandoned candy factory.
Just his style.

56:24.660 --> 56:26.335
Wayne, I think
I've got something.

56:26.360 --> 56:29.360
Download this transmission
and tell Gordon to have her men at that address.

56:29.800 --> 56:32.740
- I'm gonna--
- Aren't you the nasty tattletale?

56:32.860 --> 56:36.200
Ratting me out
before I have my fun.

56:36.460 --> 56:38.200
Papa spank!

56:57.090 --> 56:58.080
Yeah,
I know!

57:43.260 --> 57:45.800
I'd better sit down
before I bust a gut!

57:47.080 --> 57:48.880
Catch you later, kiddo!

57:53.220 --> 57:55.240
It's stopped.
I'm going after him.

58:17.970 --> 58:18.640
Gotcha!

58:42.580 --> 58:43.280
Ace.

58:55.700 --> 58:57.180
Good Bat-dog.

59:07.480 --> 59:08.580
Where'd he go?

59:13.520 --> 59:14.360
Watch it!

59:14.900 --> 59:15.760
You watch it!

59:18.460 --> 59:18.980
It's him!

59:39.180 --> 59:39.920
Double down.

59:58.240 --> 01:00:00.800
Lovely playroom.
You getting this, Wayne?

01:00:01.160 --> 01:00:04.100
I see it.
You keep your eyes open for the Joker.

01:00:14.860 --> 01:00:15.710
Tim.

01:00:16.320 --> 01:00:17.560
Get up, Drake.

01:00:19.160 --> 01:00:21.000
What? Who is it?

01:00:21.460 --> 01:00:23.040
Where's the Joker?

01:00:23.300 --> 01:00:24.250
Joker?

01:00:24.400 --> 01:00:26.980
Drop the act.
I know you're working with him.

01:00:27.800 --> 01:00:31.130
No, Joker's gone.
I don't know where he is, really.

01:00:31.680 --> 01:00:34.540
The suit sensors aren't picking up
any pulse fluctuations.

01:00:35.080 --> 01:00:36.300
He's telling the truth.

01:00:36.580 --> 01:00:39.980
I don't do this anymore.
I have a home and family.

01:00:40.060 --> 01:00:43.900
I gave this up years ago.
Kids' stuff. That's all it was.

01:00:44.660 --> 01:00:47.160
He may be telling the truth,
but he's still whacked.

01:00:47.620 --> 01:00:51.120
Fun and games.
Boy Wonder playing the hero.

01:00:51.200 --> 01:00:54.200
Fighting the bad guys
and no one ever gets--

01:00:54.700 --> 01:00:56.700
Oh, God.

01:00:57.080 --> 01:00:58.700
I killed him.

01:00:59.180 --> 01:01:00.700
I didn't mean to.

01:01:01.080 --> 01:01:02.930
I tried so hard to forget.

01:01:03.160 --> 01:01:07.300
But I still hear the shot,
still see his dead smile.

01:01:07.880 --> 01:01:09.810
Every night
the dreams get stronger.

01:01:09.960 --> 01:01:12.540
He's there when I sleep,
whispering, laughing...

01:01:12.700 --> 01:01:15.780
...telling me I'm just as bad as he is,
we're both the same.

01:01:16.080 --> 01:01:17.700
I'm calling an ambulance.

01:01:18.000 --> 01:01:20.580
No, I'm all right.
Forgive me, Terry.

01:01:20.640 --> 01:01:24.400
Old, nasty memories
twisting inside me like bad oysters.

01:01:24.760 --> 01:01:25.780
Nothing really.

01:01:26.220 --> 01:01:27.800
I'm perfectly fine now.

01:01:28.240 --> 01:01:29.700
How do you know my name?

01:01:30.100 --> 01:01:33.080
There's nothing about you
I don't know, Bat-fake.

01:01:38.410 --> 01:01:39.670
Terry!

01:01:41.410 --> 01:01:43.200
Have a time-out, kid.

01:01:43.340 --> 01:01:45.780
Can't let you
spoil the party too soon.

01:01:46.150 --> 01:01:50.740
And Bruce, I'm sure you've got
your monkey-boy wired somehow.

01:01:51.400 --> 01:01:55.200
That's just peachy, because I want you
to see every minute of this.

01:01:55.690 --> 01:01:57.100
It's a killer.

01:02:15.400 --> 01:02:16.670
My God.

01:02:20.580 --> 01:02:23.700
Oh, I never get tired of that!

01:02:24.280 --> 01:02:25.300
Drake?

01:02:25.750 --> 01:02:27.080
You're the Joker?

01:02:27.890 --> 01:02:32.260
That flabby oaf doesn't even realize
I'm using him as a time-share.

01:02:32.440 --> 01:02:36.690
Beneath this puckish exterior
lies the mind of a genius...

01:02:36.900 --> 01:02:38.400
...years ahead of my time.

01:02:38.780 --> 01:02:41.670
In the weeks young Robin
was under my tutelage...

01:02:41.860 --> 01:02:45.980
...l used him as the subject
of my greatest experiment.

01:02:46.520 --> 01:02:49.600
Utilizing cutting-edge
genetics technology...

01:02:49.810 --> 01:02:51.710
...which I had pinched
here and there...

01:02:51.880 --> 01:02:54.940
...l encoded my DNA
on a microchip...

01:02:55.100 --> 01:02:58.380
...and set it
into bird-boy's birdbrain.

01:02:58.850 --> 01:03:00.240
Here.

01:03:00.540 --> 01:03:05.120
Everything that was me has been
a-sleeping all comfy and cozy...

01:03:05.360 --> 01:03:08.240
...inside Tim Drake's subconscious.

01:03:08.460 --> 01:03:12.280
At first, I had to limit the time
I spent in Drake's body.

01:03:12.720 --> 01:03:14.400
He's not aware of what I do...

01:03:14.560 --> 01:03:17.500
...chalking up any lingering memories
to bad dreams.

01:03:17.770 --> 01:03:21.140
If his family misses him,
I simply call wifey and tell her:

01:03:21.320 --> 01:03:22.860
"l'm working late, honey."

01:03:23.660 --> 01:03:25.640
The changes come at will now...

01:03:25.860 --> 01:03:30.100
...and soon I'll be strong enough
to live in this body permanently.

01:03:30.250 --> 01:03:33.120
Mr. J's on the rebound, baby!

01:03:33.320 --> 01:03:37.350
My comeback party's gonna
set the whole town on fire!

01:03:59.920 --> 01:04:02.380
So where should I
make ground zero?

01:04:02.520 --> 01:04:06.810
Gotham General, where our hero's
dear little Dana is recuperating?

01:04:07.000 --> 01:04:11.480
Or here, in the happy garden
of Mrs. Mary McGinnis?

01:04:13.480 --> 01:04:16.760
I always think it adds resonance
to a hero's mission...

01:04:16.930 --> 01:04:20.120
...to have some defining element
of tragedy in his background...

01:04:20.300 --> 01:04:21.670
...don't you?

01:04:22.660 --> 01:04:26.280
Ah, but the one and only
kick-off point...

01:04:26.340 --> 01:04:29.070
...must be stately Wayne Manor.

01:04:29.400 --> 01:04:30.600
Gone in a flash...

01:04:30.710 --> 01:04:34.660
...before Brucie can hobble to safety
or mount a rescue.

01:04:35.280 --> 01:04:36.580
Don't worry, though.

01:04:39.520 --> 01:04:42.100
I'll be hitting those other spots
soon enough.

01:04:43.640 --> 01:04:45.360
Adiós, Brucie.

01:04:45.590 --> 01:04:49.120
I guess I should salute you
as a worthy adversary and all that...

01:04:49.160 --> 01:04:52.900
...but the truth is,
I really did hate your guts.

01:04:55.270 --> 01:04:59.760
What about it, kid?
Any last words for the old Bat-fart?

01:05:00.320 --> 01:05:01.860
Yeah.
Sic him.

01:05:08.660 --> 01:05:09.940
Ace, here!

01:05:13.880 --> 01:05:14.920
Attaboy!

01:05:27.930 --> 01:05:30.080
End of the line, Snoopy.

01:05:36.810 --> 01:05:37.640
No!

01:05:52.940 --> 01:05:54.520
Oh, good.

01:05:54.700 --> 01:05:56.300
The beam's headed here.

01:05:56.460 --> 01:05:59.000
Now I'll have to start
all over again.

01:05:59.330 --> 01:06:02.620
Thanks for wrecking everything, kid.
See you around.

01:06:03.040 --> 01:06:03.820
Hold it.

01:06:04.900 --> 01:06:06.900
Oh, wise up, junior.

01:06:06.960 --> 01:06:08.340
Game's over!

01:06:08.540 --> 01:06:11.070
- I'm taking you in.
- Right.

01:06:17.850 --> 01:06:19.910
You're out of your league, McGinnis.

01:06:20.120 --> 01:06:24.540
I know every trick the original Batman and Robin
knew at their peak.

01:06:25.480 --> 01:06:27.940
Maybe, but you don't know
a thing about me.

01:06:28.330 --> 01:06:29.350
You?

01:06:29.560 --> 01:06:31.540
What's to know?
You're a punk.

01:06:31.660 --> 01:06:33.290
A rank amateur.

01:06:33.440 --> 01:06:37.770
A costumed errand boy taking orders
from a senile old man.

01:06:37.860 --> 01:06:40.400
Still, if it's the whooping
you're a-wanting...

01:06:42.340 --> 01:06:45.700
That's right.
Better to run and save yourself.

01:06:45.760 --> 01:06:47.620
That's about your speed.

01:06:49.950 --> 01:06:51.360
Let's dance, bozo.

01:07:07.340 --> 01:07:09.780
He's tough.
Any suggestions, boss?

01:07:09.860 --> 01:07:13.240
Joker is vain and likes to talk.
He'll try to distract you, but don't listen.

01:07:13.340 --> 01:07:15.280
Block it out
and power on through.

01:07:15.340 --> 01:07:16.370
Wait.

01:07:16.580 --> 01:07:18.010
I like to talk too.

01:07:21.310 --> 01:07:23.650
- What are you doing?
- Fighting dirty!

01:07:23.800 --> 01:07:26.120
The real Batman would never--

01:07:26.520 --> 01:07:28.680
Told you, you didn't know me.

01:07:30.860 --> 01:07:32.900
Funny guy.

01:07:33.390 --> 01:07:34.660
Can't say the same for you.

01:07:36.760 --> 01:07:40.240
Impudent brat.
Who do you think you're talking to?

01:07:40.640 --> 01:07:42.320
Not a comedian,
I'll tell ya that.

01:07:43.870 --> 01:07:44.820
Shut your mouth!

01:07:46.510 --> 01:07:49.100
The real Batman
never talked to you much, did he?

01:07:49.360 --> 01:07:51.660
That's probably why you were
so fixated on him.

01:07:53.310 --> 01:07:56.300
Don't play psychoanalyst
with me, boy!

01:07:56.680 --> 01:07:58.800
Oh, I don't need a degree
to figure you out.

01:08:02.240 --> 01:08:03.935
The real reason
you kept coming back...

01:08:03.960 --> 01:08:06.000
...was you never got a laugh
out of the old man.

01:08:06.990 --> 01:08:08.980
I'm not hearing this.

01:08:09.030 --> 01:08:11.980
Get a clue, clownie.
He's got no sense of humor.

01:08:12.080 --> 01:08:14.140
He wouldn't know a good joke
if it bit him in the cape.

01:08:15.170 --> 01:08:18.600
- Not that you ever had a good joke.
- Shut up. Shut up!

01:08:18.640 --> 01:08:21.520
I mean, joy buzzers,
squirting flowers? Lame!

01:08:21.660 --> 01:08:25.610
Where's the A material? Make a face,
drop your pants, something!

01:08:25.810 --> 01:08:27.020
Show yourself!

01:08:27.080 --> 01:08:30.660
You make me laugh, but only cause
I think you're kind of pathetic.

01:08:33.490 --> 01:08:34.980
Stop that!

01:08:36.560 --> 01:08:39.435
You fell in a tank of acid,
got your skin bleached...

01:08:39.460 --> 01:08:41.390
...then decided to become a super villain.

01:08:41.590 --> 01:08:43.740
What? You couldn't get work
as a rodeo clown?

01:08:47.930 --> 01:08:49.560
Don't you dare laugh at me!

01:08:52.170 --> 01:08:55.520
Why? I thought the Joker
always wanted to make Batman laugh.

01:08:55.840 --> 01:08:57.330
You're not Batman!

01:09:23.240 --> 01:09:24.760
Come on, McGinnis!

01:09:24.880 --> 01:09:28.280
Laugh it up now,
you miserable little punk! Laugh!

01:09:30.360 --> 01:09:33.940
I can't hear you!

01:09:34.380 --> 01:09:36.600
Ha ha!

01:10:04.780 --> 01:10:06.220
Easy, I've got you.

01:10:16.260 --> 01:10:17.420
Way ahead of you, mutt.

01:11:10.440 --> 01:11:13.440
Delia and Deidre Dennis,
your grandmother has paid your bail...

01:11:13.480 --> 01:11:16.300
...and you're being released into her custody,
pending your trial.

01:11:16.540 --> 01:11:18.000
- Oh.
- Joy.

01:11:21.920 --> 01:11:23.820
You rotten little scamps!

01:11:23.920 --> 01:11:28.000
I struggle to make a good home for you
and this is the thanks I get!

01:11:29.560 --> 01:11:31.080
Break a grandmother's heart!

01:11:31.140 --> 01:11:35.620
- I hope they throw the book at you!
- Oh, shut up, Nana Harley.

01:11:39.900 --> 01:11:41.900
You didn't have to
cover up for me, Barbara.

01:11:42.210 --> 01:11:45.680
The Joker's gone, Tim.
You were just along for the ride.

01:11:47.710 --> 01:11:48.910
How are you doing, Mr. Drake?

01:11:49.180 --> 01:11:51.100
Tim,
this is Terry McGinnis.

01:11:51.340 --> 01:11:53.800
- We met the other night.
- We did?

01:11:56.760 --> 01:11:58.300
I owe you big time.

01:11:58.840 --> 01:11:59.820
Forget it.

01:12:00.090 --> 01:12:04.500
For what it's worth, Bruce couldn't have chosen
anyone better to put on the mask.

01:12:05.330 --> 01:12:07.900
Coming from you,
that means everything.

01:12:08.730 --> 01:12:11.500
Sometimes the important things
go unsaid.

01:12:12.240 --> 01:12:15.715
If there's one thing I've learned,
you've got to appreciate the people in your life...

01:12:15.740 --> 01:12:17.340
...while you have the chance.

01:12:17.680 --> 01:12:20.470
Not everyone is capable
of expressing that, Tim.

01:12:20.680 --> 01:12:23.340
No matter how much
they might feel it in their heart.

01:12:23.950 --> 01:12:25.080
I know.

01:12:29.520 --> 01:12:30.420
What are you doing here?

01:12:30.890 --> 01:12:32.420
It's where I should be.

01:12:35.990 --> 01:12:36.840
Terry.

01:12:38.600 --> 01:12:41.100
I've been thinking about
what you once told me...

01:12:42.200 --> 01:12:43.180
...and you were wrong.

01:12:44.340 --> 01:12:46.440
It's not Batman
that makes you worthwhile.

01:12:47.840 --> 01:12:49.500
It's the other way around.

01:12:50.170 --> 01:12:52.360
Never tell yourself
anything different.

01:12:53.680 --> 01:12:54.600
Thanks.

01:13:02.820 --> 01:13:04.000
Hello, Tim.

01:13:05.520 --> 01:13:07.250
Hi, old man.
